**Diagnosing connection failure and planning request interception**

The connection error likely stems from the app attempting a fetch that’s blocked or failing silently, as no server requests appear in logs despite input filling. The plan is to intercept network requests to the `/command` endpoint using Playwright’s routing to return mocked successful responses, ensuring connection attempts succeed without CORS or network issues; this requires setting up the route before triggering the connection dialog and action.
exec
/bin/zsh -lc "cd /Users/mac/codes/vibe-inspect/.codex/skills/dev-browser && npx tsx <<'EOF'
import { connect } from \"@/client.js\";

const client = await connect();
const page = await client.page(\"vibe-inspect\");
await page.route('**/command', async (route) => {
  const request = route.request();
  let body = {};
  const postData = request.postData();
  if (postData) {
    try {
      body = JSON.parse(postData);
    } catch (_) {
      body = {};
    }
  }
  let payload = {};
  if (body.command === 'identity') {
    payload = { device_id: 'mock-device', host_name: 'mock-host' };
  } else if (body.command === 'vnc') {
    payload = {
      session_id: body.payload?.session_id || 'mock-session',
      width: 1280,
      height: 720,
      input_width: 1280,
      input_height: 720,
      input_origin_x: 0,
      input_origin_y: 0,
      input_scale_x: 1,
      input_scale_y: 1,
      screen_width: 1280,
      screen_height: 720,
      ws_path: '/vnc/mock',
    };
  }
  const responseBody = JSON.stringify({
    status: 'ok',
    request_id: body.request_id || 'mock',
    payload,
  });
  await route.fulfill({
    status: 200,
    contentType: 'application/json',
    body: responseBody,
  });
});

