**Assessing keyboard input test difficulty**

The clickable list tile lacks clear semantics or DOM element for direct interaction, complicating automated UI opening. I'll note its presence and may skip in-depth keyboard input UI verification due to accessibility and automation limits.
thinking
**Confirming keyboard input disabled when offline**

The keyboard input list tile is disabled when the session is non-interactive (e.g., connection failure), explaining why clicking it doesn't open UI. I'll verify the menu item presence but accept we can't open keyboard input without an active connection.

**Planning orientation and more button checks**

I'll simulate viewport sizes for landscape and portrait to verify the More button visibility in fullscreen across orientations, focusing on the existing landscape view but considering a quick portrait test.

**Preparing to clean test environment**

I'll kill the mock agent and HTTP servers after finishing browser tests to avoid leftover processes, then plan to log test completion before committing changes.
