**Defining progress entry format**

I'm settling on a progress log entry format with timestamp, optional thread ID, run details, commit info, and post-commit status; progress entries will reference the relevant commit and be appended after the final commit to ensure accurate status.
thinking
**Clarifying dual-commit process and test logging**

The first commit includes code changes while the second holds progress log updates referencing the first commit hash; post-commit status in the progress entry reflects after the final (second) commit. I'm preparing to rerun the exact HTTP server command to confirm a clean PASS and neatly document test results including partial failures.
